   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Calculate <span data-math=\"\\frac{2}{5} \\div \\frac{3}{{10}} + \\frac{1}{6}\">\\frac{2}{5} \\div \\frac{3}{{10}} + \\frac{1}{6}</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{2}{5} \\div \\frac{3}{{10}} + \\frac{1}{6}\"></span></p>\n<p>Use PEMDAS. Do the division first by multiplying by the reciprocal.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{2}{5} \\times \\frac{{10}}{3} + \\frac{1}{6}\"></span></p>\n<p>Multiply the numerators and denominators, dividing out common factors.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{2}{{\\cancel{5}}} \\times \\frac{{2 \\times \\cancel{5}}}{3} + \\frac{1}{6}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{4}{3} + \\frac{1}{6}\"></span></p>\n<p>Rewrite the first fraction to have 6 in the denominator.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{4 \\times 2}}{{3 \\times 2}} + \\frac{1}{6}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{8}{6} + \\frac{1}{6}\"></span></p>\n<p>Add the numerators.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{9}{6}\"></span></p>\n<p>Divide out common factors.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{3 \\times \\cancel{3}}}{{2 \\times \\cancel{3}}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{3}{2}\"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\,\\frac{3}{2}\">\\,\\frac{3}{2}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
